{"id": 67, "ts": 1780661610.4425867, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit.\u202fJames has confirmed that we have no concrete examples of C\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation or professional communication, but the same is true for Candidate\u202fB\u2014and B\u2019s profile actually includes explicit negative indicators: he is \u201cpretentious,\u201d \u201cgrumpy,\u201d and \u201cuncooperative,\u201d and we also know his memory for numbers is weak, threatening attention to detail.\u202fIn contrast, C\u2019s only communication\u2011related concerns are \u201cdifficulty communicating ideas\u201d and being \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d while he also \u201cputs concern for others above everything\u201d and demonstrates excellent attention skills, rapid correct decision\u2011making, calmness under crisis, and strong technical competence.\u202fGiven that the core safety criteria (decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence) are clearly met by C, and his interpersonal profile, though imperfect, is less likely to undermine crew cooperation than B\u2019s documented uncooperative behavior, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
