{"id": 71, "ts": 1780661662.518642, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019ve reconsidered my position in light of the cumulative evidence. While Candidate\u202fB\u2019s conscientiousness and stress\u2011handling are valuable, we still have no concrete examples of his crew\u2011cooperation, and the documented \u201cpretentious,\u201d \u201cgrumpy,\u201d and \u201cuncooperative\u201d behaviours raise serious doubts about his ability to maintain a collaborative cockpit environment\u2014especially given his weak memory for numbers, which threatens attention to detail. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is explicitly noted as 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, and puts concern for others above everything, directly addressing our crew\u2011cooperation and responsibility criteria. Although C has communication difficulties and is perceived as egocentric, these concerns are identified but not shown to have caused safety\u2011relevant failures, and they appear less detrimental than B\u2019s documented interpersonal deficits. Therefore, I now recommend Candidate\u202fC as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
